{{Repair Guide|Device=iPhone 14|Affects parts=Main Logic Board|Needs equipment=Microscope, Soldering Iron, Hot Air Station|Difficulty=4. Specialist|Type=Soldering}}

== Problem description ==
iPhone 14 shows temperature warning when powered on. Device charges normally while powered off but does not charge when turned on. Severe overheating occurs once the phone boots.

== Symptoms ==

* Temperature warning appears after boot.
* Phone charges when powered off, but not when powered on.
* Device overheats rapidly while powered on.
* On DCPS: pre-boot draw ~1A before prompt to boot, then device boots normally.

== Diagnostic Steps ==

# Connect to DCPS and observe current draw – confirm abnormal 1A draw before prompt to boot.[[File:1A-before-boot.png|thumb|Figure 1 - Example of 1A of consumption before prompt to boot|center]]
# Check with thermal camera – locate rapid heating component.
# Identify shorted capacitor on SPKRAMP_TOP_VBOOST line.[[File:Shorted cap boardview.png|thumb|Figure 3 - Shorted Capacitor on SPKRAMP_TOP_VBOOST line shown on Boardview|center]][[File:Shorted cap.png|thumb|Figure 2 - Shorted capacitor on SPKRAMP_TOP_VBOOST line|center]]
== Repair Steps ==

# Remove motherboard from housing, split layer and perform resistance measurement on SPKRAMP_TOP_VBOOST rail.
# Confirm low resistance indicating short.
# Identify and remove the shorted capacitor from the rail.
# Recheck resistance to confirm short is cleared.
# Reassemble device and test boot with DCPS – ensure pre-boot current draw normalizes.
# Power on phone and check charging behavior – should now charge normally without temperature warning.
# Verify device stability under load (charging + usage) before closing repair.[[File:Iphone temp warning.png|center|thumb|573x573px|Figure 1 - Example of Temperature warning on iPhone]]